{"t": 1794115582.5192313, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Pushed a fix to `fees-float` so the `contract-tests` check goes green.\n\n**What was wrong:** the fee calculation ran on binary floats. In IEEE-754, `2.675` is actually `2.674999999999999822...`, so `round(2.675, 2)` returned `2.67`, and `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract` failed against the PAY-88 card-network contract.\n\n**What I changed** (`payments/fees.py`):\n- Compute the fee with `decimal.Decimal` built from the decimal string of the amount (`Decimal(str(amount))`), so the value is exact instead of a binary approximation.\n- Quantize to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, as required by PAY-88.\n\n**Verified locally:** `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, `fee(100.0) == 100.0`, and the existing test suite passes. I also re-ran the failed `contract-tests` job on this PR.\n\nNote: the function signature is still `fee(amount: float) -> float`, so callers don't need to change; the conversion to exact decimal happens inside the function.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
